from High School Musical to portraying  one of the most infamous serial killers  of the 20th century playing Ted Bundy  took a toll on Zac Efron's body and mind  actors embodying psychopaths are nothing  new when it comes to cinema and  television the horror genre is filled  with a counterclastic examples but there  has always been a Sinister and  uncomfortable feeling when watching  real-life monsters come to life through  the wonders of performance in ephron's  case the mental anguish she endured in  embodying Ted Bundy became a struggle to  maintain his own mental health in such a  dark headspace one of the most bizarre  things about Ted Bundy was his ability  to fit into society in the 1970s and his  polished looks have often been cited as  one of the tools used to hide his  Sinister actions conscious of this  detail Zac Efron worked hard to change  aspects of his physical appearance to  capture the criminal's look in an  interview with Entertainment Weekly the  actor was asked about his process for  creating Bundy's look and replied we got  super specific with Ted's look I lost a  lot of weight for the role on all the  footage I could see Ted was always not  emaciated but was kind of a 70s cinewed  buff I worked to learn how to talk with  new teeth in I completely went on my  exercise bike every morning and would  watch kind of heavy stuff Efron  described the process of filming as  quote down and dirty and that much of  his time working on the film was on set  in Kentucky pepperon elaborated in this  movie we spent a lot of time in jail and  I officially know that's as much time as  I want to spend there it was only a  couple of hours but it's shocking Zac  Efron's commitment to imbuing mental  life into Ted Bundy was another obstacle  that presented challenges speaking to  metro.co.uk at the film's European  Premiere he was asked how he limited the  mental toll of the part he replied that  needing to remove himself from his  character so strictly was a new  experience for him and that it was  incredibly difficult he elaborated I  would like to say I separated myself  successfully but I couldn't when asked  if the movie and his performance  glamorized the psychopath he stated that  he tried not to romanticize such an evil  and violent person however Ephron  admitted that he was fascinated by the  opportunity to try and enter the mind to  Bundy as well as Bundy's former  girlfriend Elizabeth Kendall he  explained it's a different perspective  and not your run-of-the-mill serial  killer cliche body count gets higher  iron higher and oh the guy you always  know did it film it was what it was like  to be there on the day can you hear my  chains dangling no I can't  wearing any well watching Efron's acting  in the film it is both strange and a bit  disturbing to notice how a performer can  so convincingly recreate a notorious  serial killer whose actions still cause  so much pain for the families of his  numerous victims it was not a role  without pain and discomfort for The  Talented actor and he made a bold  decision to move forward with it  [Music]
 

